    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Aurora Innovation, Inc. is a public company headquartered in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, trading under the ticker AUR. Its website describes it as a self-driving freight company, with its core offering being the Aurora Driver, a system it says combines hardware and software backed by verifiable AI and can be integrated into a customer's fleet. The company frames its aim as delivering self-driving technology safely, quickly, and broadly.\n\nThe site's material is largely customer and partner testimony rather than product detail. A Werner representative describes a pilot program hauling freight autonomously between Fort Worth and El Paso, using a hybrid model of Werner professional drivers and the Aurora Driver. A Volvo representative says the Aurora Driver is integrated into the Volvo VNL Autonomous, and cites a projection that freight volumes will grow five fold between 2010-2050. Another quote credits the system with strong performance over millions of autonomous miles.\n\nThe held facts add little beyond corporate identity. Aurora is recorded as a for-profit public company with CIK 0001828108, and its recorded legal exposure is in Pennsylvania, with a count of 170. No lawsuits, no tracked products, and no MCP servers are listed.",
